<div class="doc-info">
    <h3 class="doc-h3">What this is</h3>
    <p class="doc-body">This is the <strong>Docker &amp; Kubernetes coordinator</strong> — the entry point for every plan that touches
    containers, images, orchestration, and the path to Kubernetes. It does <strong>not</strong> replace the app-wide
    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/MASTER_PLAN') %]">Master Plan</a>; it is the Docker/K8s slice of it, so the container
    work has one navigable artifact instead of a dozen disconnected docs. Each linked plan remains the authoritative spec for its own work.</p>
</div>

<div id="purpose">
    <h2 class="doc-h2">0. Purpose &amp; scope</h2>
    <p class="doc-body">Group the container-related plans by function and make their dependencies explicit:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Strategy / architecture</strong> — the long-range Docker→K8s direction.</li>
        <li><strong>Orchestration / HA</strong> — Kubernetes clusters, app deployment manifests, failover, DB HA.</li>
        <li><strong>Deployment &amp; secrets</strong> — production deploy flow, DB-config fallback, image/secret hygiene.</li>
        <li><strong>Diagnostics</strong> — container build / port failure reports.</li>
        <li><strong>Dev environment</strong> — running Comserv in Docker for development.</li>
        <li><strong>Agents</strong> — the Docker coding-agent spec.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#purpose">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
</div>

<div id="index">
    <h2 class="doc-h2">1. Plan index (verified routes)</h2>
    <p class="doc-muted">Every link below was confirmed against <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Documentation.pm</code>
    (<code>sub view :Path('/Documentation') :Args(1)</code> + flat basename match). Routes are
    <code>/Documentation/&lt;Key&gt;</code> — no subdirectory, no <code>.tt</code> extension.</p>

