<div id="sequencing">
    <h2 class="doc-h2">2. Sequencing at a glance</h2>
    <div class="doc-codebox"><pre>
STRATEGY  DOCKER_KUBERNETES_MIGRATION_STRATEGY ─┐
                                                │
READINESS Phase0KubernetesReadinessPlan ────────┤
                                                │
ORCH      K3S_APP_HA_PLAN (#202) ───────────────┤  (Kubernetes PRIMARY)
           ├─ PRODUCTION_DB_KUBERNETES_MIGRATION_PLAN
           ├─ K3S_PRODUCTION_MIGRATION_GUIDE
           └─ COMSERV_INFRASTRUCTURE_MIGRATION_AMENDMENT
                                                │
DEPLOY     DEPLOY_WORKFLOW ─────────────────────┤  (authoritative; supersedes REBUILD_AND_DEPLOY_INSTRUCTIONS)
           ProductionDeployment
           DockerSecretsFallbackDebuggingPlan
           dev_isolation_and_backups_plan
                                                │
OPS        docker_container_prod_build_failure_diagnostics
           docker_container_port_3000_diagnostics
           docker_pycharm_setup_guide
           docker-agent-guide
                                                │
EDGE       GatewayPlan · CREDENTIALS_AUDIT_AND_PLAN (#239 IMGSEC)
</pre></div>
    <p class="doc-muted">Note: this is a <em>view</em> of the work, not a fresh scheduling wave. The migration family is large and partly
    superseded by the canonical Deploy Workflow — confirm which are still live before investing.</p>
    <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#sequencing">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
</div>

<div id="overlaps">
    <h2 class="doc-h2">3. Overlaps &amp; supersession</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>K3S_APP_HA_PLAN (#202 INFRA-HA)</strong> is the live HA authority. Where its orchestration steps
            conflict with <code>DOCKER_KUBERNETES_MIGRATION_STRATEGY</code>, follow K3S_APP_HA_PLAN.</li>
        <li><strong>DEPLOY_WORKFLOW</strong> supersedes <code>REBUILD_AND_DEPLOY_INSTRUCTIONS</code> (the latter is
            marked superseded on disk — not linked as active above).</li>
        <li><strong>CREDENTIALS_AUDIT_AND_PLAN</strong> carries <strong>#239 IMGSEC</strong> (Docker image credential leak
            remediation) — coordinate Docker secret work there, not in a standalone doc.</li>
        <li><strong>GatewayPlan</strong> overlaps where containers are edge-exposed; keep ingress decisions consistent with
            K3S_APP_HA_PLAN's "OPNsense = edge only if configured" stance.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#overlaps">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
</div>

